module

public import TauCeti.GroupTheory.Presentation.GroupPresentation

/-!
# A transcribed presentation of the O'Nan sporadic group

This file carries the `ONan` row of the sporadic presentation data required by milestone S1 of
`TauCetiRoadmap/CFSGStatement/README.md`. It records `GPLTable.ON.1` from Roderik Lindenbergh's
Group Presentations Library as a `TauCeti.GroupPresentation`, together with the exact source,
generator convention, transcription notes, expected counts, and decidable checks on the
transcription.

The presentation starts with the Coxeter path

```text
a --3-- b --3-- c --8-- d --3-- e --3-- f.
```

Thus `a` through `f` are involutions, the five displayed products have the indicated orders, and
every omitted pair among these six generators has product of order two. The source then adds a
seventh generator `g` and the eight relations

```text
g^4,  af = g^2,  af = (cd)^4,  c c^(dgdg),  d d^(cgcg),  (bcdg)^5,
g b g^c g^b g^c,  g e g^d g^e g^d.
```

Here the source uses `x^y = y^-1 x y`, and its decoder compiles an equality `x = y` to the relator
`x^-1 y`. The Coxeter path contributes six square relations and fifteen pair relations, so the
complete list has `21 + 8 = 29` relators.

The proved metadata theorem checks the generator and relator counts. Two further decidable checks
show that the compiled words contain `172` signed letters and are cyclically reduced. As a separate
transcription check, GAP 4.15.1 enumerates `122760` cosets of the subgroup generated by `a` through
`f`, agreeing with the index of the `L3(7):2` subgroup recorded by GPL. This computation is
provenance rather than a Lean theorem: this file asserts no order, finiteness, simplicity, or
identification result. A separate source-to-Lean read-through remains part of the S1 review
artifact required by the roadmap.

## Main definition

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.onanPresentation`: the GPL finite presentation of the O'Nan sporadic group.

## References

* R. Lindenbergh, *Group Presentations Library*, version 1.0, record `GPLTable.ON.1`,
  <https://doris.tudelft.nl/~rlindenbergh/GPL/gpl.g>.
* C. E. Praeger and L. H. Soicher, *Low Rank Representations and Graphs for Sporadic Groups*,
  Cambridge University Press, 1997, Chapter 4, doi:10.1017/CBO9780511526039.005.
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti.Sporadic

private abbrev a : Relator (Fin 7) := .gen 0

private abbrev b : Relator (Fin 7) := .gen 1

private abbrev c : Relator (Fin 7) := .gen 2

private abbrev d : Relator (Fin 7) := .gen 3

private abbrev e : Relator (Fin 7) := .gen 4

private abbrev f : Relator (Fin 7) := .gen 5

private abbrev g : Relator (Fin 7) := .gen 6

@[inherit_doc Relator.mul]
local infixl:70 " ⬝ " => Relator.mul

/-- The source conjugate `r^s = s^-1 r s`. -/
private abbrev sourceConj (r s : Relator (Fin 7)) : Relator (Fin 7) :=
  .inv s ⬝ r ⬝ s

/-- The six involution relations and the fifteen pair relations decoded from the Coxeter path
`a3b3c8d3e3f` in `GPLTable.ON.1`.

The ten nonedges are written explicitly with exponent two, so this list records the complete
Coxeter matrix rather than relying on an implicit default. -/
private def onanCoxeterRelators : List (Relator (Fin 7)) :=
  [ .pow a 2,
    .pow b 2,
    .pow c 2,
    .pow d 2,
    .pow e 2,
    .pow f 2,
    .pow (a ⬝ b) 3,
    .pow (b ⬝ c) 3,
    .pow (c ⬝ d) 8,
    .pow (d ⬝ e) 3,
    .pow (e ⬝ f) 3,
    .pow (a ⬝ c) 2,
    .pow (a ⬝ d) 2,
    .pow (a ⬝ e) 2,
    .pow (a ⬝ f) 2,
    .pow (b ⬝ d) 2,
    .pow (b ⬝ e) 2,
    .pow (b ⬝ f) 2,
    .pow (c ⬝ e) 2,
    .pow (c ⬝ f) 2,
    .pow (d ⬝ f) 2 ]

/-- The eight words following the Coxeter path in `GPLTable.ON.1`.

The source decoder represents an equality `x = y` by the relator `x^-1 y`, explaining the leading
inverses in the second and third entries. The other entries preserve the source's conjugation
convention `x^y = y^-1 x y`. -/
private def onanAdditionalRelators : List (Relator (Fin 7)) :=
  [ .pow g 4,
    .inv (a ⬝ f) ⬝ .pow g 2,
    .inv (a ⬝ f) ⬝ .pow (c ⬝ d) 4,
    c ⬝ sourceConj c (d ⬝ g ⬝ d ⬝ g),
    d ⬝ sourceConj d (c ⬝ g ⬝ c ⬝ g),
    .pow (b ⬝ c ⬝ d ⬝ g) 5,
    g ⬝ b ⬝ sourceConj g c ⬝ sourceConj g b ⬝ sourceConj g c,
    g ⬝ e ⬝ sourceConj g d ⬝ sourceConj g e ⬝ sourceConj g d ]

/-- The Group Presentations Library finite presentation `GPLTable.ON.1` of the O'Nan sporadic
group on generators `a`, `b`, `c`, `d`, `e`, `f`, and `g`.

The source describes this as a full presentation of the abstract group and identifies its origin
as Praeger--Soicher. No structural property of the presented group is asserted here: this
definition records only the cited generators and relations. -/
def onanPresentation : GroupPresentation where
  generatorNames := ["a", "b", "c", "d", "e", "f", "g"]
  source := "R. Lindenbergh, Group Presentations Library, version 1.0; presentation attributed \
    there to C. E. Praeger and L. H. Soicher, Low Rank Representations and Graphs for Sporadic \
    Groups, Cambridge University Press, 1997"
  sourceLocator := "GPLTable.ON.1 in \
    https://doris.tudelft.nl/~rlindenbergh/GPL/gpl.g; Praeger--Soicher, Chapter 4, \
    doi:10.1017/CBO9780511526039.005"
  generatorConvention := "Generators have source order a,b,c,d,e,f,g, so indices 0 through 6 \
    have those names. The Coxeter path makes a through f involutions, a labeled edge x-m-y \
    declares (x*y)^m = 1, and an omitted edge declares (x*y)^2 = 1. Products are read left to \
    right, x^y means y^-1*x*y, and the source decoder compiles x = y as x^-1*y."
  transcriptionNotes := "Expand the path a3b3c8d3e3f to six square relations, five \
    labeled-edge relations, and ten omitted-edge relations. Append the eight words in \
    presdef[3], compiling the two equalities and all conjugation expressions by the source's \
    MakeWordList \
    decoder. The expected relator count and total length are derived from this exact expansion. \
    GAP 4.15.1 enumerates 122760 cosets of the subgroup generated by a through f, agreeing with \
    the index of the L3(7):2 subgroup recorded by GPL. A separate source-to-Lean read-through \
    remains an S1 review obligation."
  expectedGeneratorCount := 7
  expectedRelatorCount := 29
  transcribed := onanCoxeterRelators ++ onanAdditionalRelators

/-- The generator and relator counts recorded for `ONan` agree with the transcribed data. -/
theorem onanPresentation_matchesMetadata : onanPresentation.matchesMetadata := by
  decide

/-- The compiled relators of the `ONan` presentation contain `172` signed letters in total. -/
theorem onanPresentation_totalLength : onanPresentation.totalLength = 172 := by
  simp [GroupPresentation.totalLength_def, GroupPresentation.relators_def, onanPresentation,
    onanCoxeterRelators, onanAdditionalRelators, sourceConj]

/-- Every compiled relator of the `ONan` presentation is cyclically reduced. -/
theorem onanPresentation_relatorsCyclicallyReduced :
    onanPresentation.relatorsCyclicallyReduced := by
  simp [GroupPresentation.relatorsCyclicallyReduced_iff, GroupPresentation.relators_def,
    onanPresentation, onanCoxeterRelators, onanAdditionalRelators, sourceConj,
    FreeGroup.IsCyclicallyReduced, FreeGroup.invRev]

end TauCeti.Sporadic
